     "text": "The kernel copies `A` straight from HBM to HBM with `nisa.dma_copy` in a single pass, without staging through SBUF. The HBM\u2192HBM direction is not among the device-tested patterns in the reference. The reference states that `dma_copy` accepts HBM or SBUF for either side, but this file has not been run on the device.\n\n- **Split across cores:** under LNC=2 each of the two programs copies its own disjoint half of the rows. `N/2` is always a multiple of 128.\n- **Chunking:** each half is moved in independent 128-row chunks, at most 1.3 MB per DMA for `N=5120`. This lets several DMAs run at once.\n- **Edge handling:** row bounds are clipped with `min`, so nothing outside the `N*N` elements is read or written.\n- **Allocation and inputs:** the output is allocated fresh inside the kernel on every call, and `A` is never written.\n\n```python title=\"impl_nki.py\"\nimport torch\n\nimport nki\nimport nki.language as nl\nimport nki.isa as nisa\n\n\n# Rows of A moved by one DMA instruction (each row is contiguous; the chunk\n# A[r0:r0+ROWS_PER_DMA, :] is a contiguous byte range of the matrix).\nROWS_PER_DMA = 128\n\n_LAST_CONFIG = {}\n\n\n@nki.jit\ndef _matrix_copy_kernel(a, rows_per_dma):\n    R = a.shape[0]\n    C = a.shape[1]\n    # Stage 1: allocate the output (uninitialised).\n    out = nl.ndarray((R, C), dtype=a.dtype, buffer=nl.shared_hbm)\n\n    # Split the rows between the programs (2 physical cores under LNC=2).\n    n_prog = nl.num_programs()\n    pid = nl.program_id(0)\n    rows_per_prog = (R + n_prog - 1) // n_prog\n    start = pid * rows_per_prog\n    end = min(R, start + rows_per_prog)\n    n_chunks = (end - start + rows_per_dma - 1) // rows_per_dma\n\n    # Stage 2: single streaming traversal, each element moved exactly once,\n    # directly HBM -> HBM (no intermediate global scratch).\n    for c in range(n_chunks):\n        r0 = start + c * rows_per_dma\n        r1 = min(end, r0 + rows_per_dma)\n        nisa.dma_copy(dst=out[r0:r1, :], src=a[r0:r1, :])\n    return out\n\n\ndef run(A: torch.Tensor, N: int, **kwargs):\n    global _LAST_CONFIG\n    rows = int(A.shape[0])\n    cols = int(A.shape[1])\n    rows_per_dma = ROWS_PER_DMA\n    B = _matrix_copy_kernel(A, rows_per_dma)\n    n_prog_assumed = 2\n    rows_per_prog = (rows + n_prog_assumed - 1) // n_prog_assumed\n    _LAST_CONFIG = {\n        \"path\": \"hbm_to_hbm_dma\",\n        \"rows_per_dma\": rows_per_dma,\n        \"programs\": n_prog_assumed,\n        \"rows_per_program\": rows_per_prog,\n        \"dmas_per_program\": (rows_per_prog + rows_per_dma - 1) // rows_per_dma,\n        \"shape\": [rows, cols],\n    }\n    return B\n\n\ndef get_last_config() -> dict:\n    return dict(_LAST_CONFIG)\n```",
